@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch deletion-bug-repro); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:590 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "datalog: regression tests confirming apply_deletions cascades correctly (Dexpi2Imf bug investigation)" ;
    bl:number 590 ;
    bl:state bl:Open .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr590 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:591 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-21T22:22:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr590Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "User reported (manual testing against equinor/Dexpi2Imf's real RML mappings, datalog rules, and SPARQL queries -- all public, readable anonymously despite equinor's SAML org-enforcement blocking authenticated gh api access) that deletion does not properly propagate into deleting inferred facts. Rather than delegate a fresh investigation, wrote the reproduction directly, reconstructing noaka_boundary.datalog's exact rule shape (isBoundaryOf/isInPackage: transitive hasPart closure, adjacentTo self-recursion gated by NOT isBoundaryOf) as datalog::Rule values, and tested IncrementalReasoner::apply_deletions against a from-scratch full-rebuild oracle rather than hand-enumerated expected facts, since hand-deriving a transitive+negated program's closure is error-prone. Two scenarios tested: (1) cross-predicate positive cascade under deletion -- existing coverage (#541) only tested a single self-recursive predicate, never a cascade crossing predicates; (2) deleting a fact that blocks a NOT-gated body atom elsewhere, which must cause a *new* derivation as a side effect of a deletion. Both passed, with fallback_count asserted unchanged to confirm the true incremental BF path ran rather than the FALLBACK_THRESHOLD full-rebuild fallback (which would be trivially correct by construction and mask a real incremental-only bug). Also confirmed sparql_endpoint's actual call sequence (physically removing the quad from the store via store.remove_quad before calling apply_deletions, rather than leaving it present) is safe, since apply_deletions's backward phase is built purely from the reasoner's own DerivedFromIndex and never checks base-store containment. Net result: the datalog crate's core apply_deletions algorithm is ruled out as the source of the reported bug for these two scenarios; the bug (if reproducible) most likely lives in the sparql_endpoint/sparql_parser layer (DELETE WHERE with property paths, untested here), graph scoping, or predates this cycle's other deletion-path fixes. Filed as a separate tracked issue (#591) rather than closed, since no fix was made -- this PR is investigative regression-test coverage." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:590 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr590Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr590 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr590Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "An advisor review caught that the first test written only covered a pure positive cascade (deleting a fact that seeds a chain with no negation involved) -- the control case, not the case the user's domain (noaka_boundary.datalog's isBoundaryOf gating isInPackage via NOT) actually turns on. Added a second, genuinely discriminating test deleting the fact that blocks the NOT-gated rule, which is the higher-frequency real deletion in this domain (a boundary marking is exactly what an engineer edits interactively)." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered stopping after the first (passing) cross-predicate test and reporting the datalog layer clean. Rejected because a user's plain-language bug report ('deletion doesn't propagate') describes the symptom, not which direction is wrong -- passing only the easier control case would not have been a complete answer." .
